  "subtitle": "The drum machine whose pads were both the instrument and the step-sequencer grid — the pad-as-program interface",
  "why_scout_cares": "The LM-1 inverts the step-sequencer grid: instead of the TR-808's 16 parallel button rows, it gives you 12 hard-plastic pads that are BOTH the trigger pads you strike to play AND the tap-to-program grid. You program by physically tapping the drum voice you want on the step you want — a pad-as-grid hybrid that is the ancestor of the MPC's pad paradigm and the exact interactive counterpoint to the museum's TR-808. Genuinely distinct interaction model, image-rich on Commons.",
